foundry-emulators-computers (1.0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add x-emulators — LGB's Xemu suite, covering the Commodore 65 / C64DX
    prototype, MEGA65, Commodore LCD prototype, VIC-20, Enterprise 64/128,
    Primo and Videoton TV Computer. None of dosbox-x, hatari, fs-uae,
    openmsx or mame emulate the C65 usefully (MAME's c65 driver is flagged
    preliminary and leaves the $E000 ROM window unmapped), so this is the
    only working coverage for that machine in the catalogue.
  * No ROMs are bundled, so it meets this metapackage's redistribution
    criterion. Reword the intro accordingly: the set is no longer
    universe-only now that a Foundry-built package is listed.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 09:30:00 +0700

foundry-emulators-computers (1.0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add mame, dual-listed with foundry-emulators-consoles (which keeps it
    for arcade/console coverage). MAME is the only packaged emulator for
    the home computers none of dosbox-x/hatari/fs-uae/openmsx cover —
    notably the Camputers Lynx, drivers lynx48k, lynx96k and lynx128k,
    all from camputers/camplynx.cpp, verified against mame 0.285+dfsg1-1
    on ubuntu:26.04 via -listsource.
  * Document the driver-name collision: MAME's "lynx" is the Atari Lynx
    handheld (atari/lynx.cpp), not the Camputers machine. Atari Lynx
    coverage in the catalogue comes from mednafen.
  * No size or reach change: foundry-core pulls both emulator
    metapackages, so mame was already installed everywhere this ships.

 -- Foundry Linux <packages@foundrylinux.org>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

